## Context

The fuel-decomposition RAG strategy (`src/aedist/query_decomposed.py`)
was introduced to fix truncation: instead of one query for all thermal
plants, three sub-queries by fuel (coal, gas, oil/other) against the
same corpus. It does eliminate truncation — but it trades truncation
for massive hallucination.

### Evidence

False-positive rate (system-only rows in reconciliation CSVs), same
reference set, 3 runs per model:

| Model            | Baseline RAG    | Decomposed       |
|------------------|-----------------|------------------|
| gpt-5.4          | 0 / 0 / 0 %     | 45 / 40 / 52 %   |
| deepseek-v3.2    | 0 / 0 / 0 %     | 20 / — / 2 %     |
| mistral-large    | 0 / 0 / 0 %     | 7 / 25 / 10 %    |
| mistral-small    | 0 / 0 / 0 %     | 29 / 0 / 19 %    |
| gemini-flash-lt  | 59 / 6 / 75 %   | 40 / 64 / 0 %    |

Every model except flash-lite has **zero** false positives in baseline
RAG. Decomposition breaks this cleanly — gpt-5.4 jumps from 0 % FP to
40–52 %. Computed with:

```
for f in experiments/outputs/{rag,decomposed}/reconciliation_*.csv; do
  total=$(tail -n +2 "$f" | wc -l)
  fp=$(grep -c '^system_only' "$f")
  printf "%s %d/%d\n" "$(basename $f)" "$fp" "$total"
done
```

### Hallucination patterns

Three patterns in `reconciliation_gpt-5.4-run3.csv` (180 system-only
rows / 343 total, 52 %):

1. **Unit splitting** (lines 165–220): aggregate plants broken into
   per-unit rows — `An Khanh 1 Unit 1` + `An Khanh 1 Unit 2` (50 MW each)
   instead of the reference `An Khánh 1` (116 MW). Systematic across
   `Vung Ang 1`, `Duyen Hai 1`, `Thai Binh 1`, `Quang Ninh 2`.
2. **Fuel leakage**: `O Mon 1 Unit 2` (gas, 330 MW) appears in coal
   output with fuel `unknown`.
3. **Structured-output failure, line 181**: plant name literally
   `"Lai Chau is hydro"`, capacity 0 MW, fuel `coal`. The model wrote
   prose into the name field, and the extractor accepted it.

### Root cause

`src/aedist/query_decomposed.py:147-150` injects the corpus as the
system message (correct), but the sub-prompts (lines 55–77) explicitly
instruct the model to go beyond the corpus:

> Be absolutely exhaustive — include operational, under construction,
> planned, proposed, and cancelled plants.

Compare `experiments/prompts/prompt_structured.txt`, the baseline,
which is terse and makes no "be exhaustive" demand. The baseline model
stays inside the corpus. The decomposition prompts push the model to
fall back on parametric memory to satisfy "exhaustive, including
cancelled" — so it splits remembered aggregates into fake units and
fabricates half-remembered names.

Neither prompt has grounding language like "based only on the provided
documents." The baseline gets away with it; decomposition does not.

### Interaction with project_rag_truncation memory

The `project_rag_truncation.md` memory claims "decomposition is the
fix." That is wrong. Decomposition fixes truncation by hallucinating
into the blank space. Memory needs updating after this ticket closes.

## Actions

1. Patch `src/aedist/query_decomposed.py:55-77`:
   - Remove "Be absolutely exhaustive — include operational, under
     construction, planned, proposed, and cancelled plants" from all
     three sub-prompts.
   - Add grounding language: "Based only on the provided documents,
     list the COAL-FIRED thermal power plants..."
   - Keep the per-fuel scoping (that is the point of decomposition).
2. Re-run one cheap model (DeepSeek V3.2, ~$0.06 per 3-run batch) as a
   probe. Compare FP rate and recall to the unpatched run.
3. If FP drops without recall collapsing, re-run the full model set
   (gpt-5.4, deepseek, mistral-large, mistral-small, gemini-flash-lite),
   3 runs each. Budget ~$3.
4. Update `report/report.tex` section 3.11 with before/after numbers
   if the fix works, or document the failure if it does not.
5. Update `project_rag_truncation.md` memory to reflect the finding.

## Test

Run DeepSeek V3.2 with patched prompts. Pass: FP rate < 5 % and recall
≥ the previous decomposed run. Fail: either metric degrades, or the
model refuses to answer without the "exhaustive" instruction.

## Exit criteria

- Sub-prompts patched and committed.
- At least one model re-run shows FP drop without recall loss.
- Report section 3.11 updated with the finding (the prompt lesson is
  the interesting methodological result, regardless of whether the
  fix works).
- `project_rag_truncation.md` memory corrected.
